Algorithm CompileBPToCircuit(P):
  Input: Branching program P with width w, depth d, n input variables
  Output: Layered circuit C with opCount ≤ 2w²d + w

  C.depth ← d
  C.width ← w
  C.outputGate ← P.accept

  for each input x:
    // Layer 0: base case
    for v in 0..w-1:
      C.eval(x, 0, v) ← (v == P.start)

    // Layers 1..d: inductive case
    for i in 1..d:
      for v in 0..w-1:
        C.eval(x, i, v) ← OR_{u=0}^{w-1} (
          C.eval(x, i-1, u) AND edgeActive(P, x, i-1, u, v)
        )

  return C

Time: O(w²d) per input
Space: O(w) for online evaluation

Algorithm TransferMatrixProduct(P):
  Input: Tropical BP P with width w, depth d
  Output: w×w matrix M = M₀ ⊗ M₁ ⊗ ... ⊗ M_{d-1}

  M ← identity matrix (tropical)
  for i in 0..d-1:
    M ← tropical_matrix_multiply(M, transferMatrix(P, i))

  // M[start][accept] = min-cost accepting path

Time: O(w³d)
Note: Circuit simulation is O(w²d) — faster by factor w
